# Project Definition

## 1. Problem Statement

Small production lines may rely on operators to manually inspect and sort products. Manual sorting can result in inconsistent classification, slower processing, and limited production traceability.

This project develops a miniature automated sorting conveyor that detects an incoming object, classifies it, directs it to the correct output location, detects abnormal operating conditions, and records basic production information.

## 2. Project Objective

Design and build a miniature automated sorting conveyor that demonstrates industrial-style automation using sensors, a conveyor motor, a sorting actuator, operator controls, machine-state sequencing, fault detection, and production-data collection.

## 3. Functional Requirements

- **FR-01:** The system shall remain stopped until a Start command is received.
- **FR-02:** The system shall stop conveyor movement when a Stop command is received.
- **FR-03:** The system shall prevent automatic operation when the emergency-stop condition is active.
- **FR-04:** The system shall detect an object entering the conveyor.
- **FR-05:** The system shall classify each detected object into one of two predefined categories.
- **FR-06:** The system shall automatically direct the classified object to the correct output location.
- **FR-07:** The system shall confirm that the object has exited the sorting process.
- **FR-08:** The system shall detect a jam or movement timeout, stop the conveyor, and generate a fault indication.
- **FR-09:** The system shall provide automatic and manual operating modes and display machine status, operating state, production counts, and active faults.
- **FR-10:** The system shall record accepted items, rejected items, total completed cycles, and detected faults.

## 4. Version 1 Scope

### Included

- One conveyor
- One object processed at a time
- Two object classifications
- One sorting diverter
- Entry, classification, and exit detection
- Start, Stop, and Reset controls
- Automatic and Manual modes
- Emergency-stop simulation
- Basic HMI/dashboard
- Fault detection and handling
- Production counters and basic data logging

### Not Included

- Computer vision
- AI-based classification
- Multiple simultaneous objects
- Robotic pick-and-place
- Industrial safety certification
- High-speed sorting
- PLC hardware in the first version
- Cloud-based remote control
